{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong upward-regime underprediction: when the last 5–10 days show a sustained rise (higher highs / higher lows), add a positive level shift to the whole path. In these examples the miss is large and persistent (~+5 to +15 €/t), growing with horizon.",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: apply an increasing uplift with forecast step (small at days 1–3, larger at days 10–30). The model’s slope is too flat versus realized trend; correct by steepening the forward curve.",
    "Lag in trend acceleration: when price breaks above the prior 20–30d high, treat it as a regime change; do not mean-revert. Increase near-term drift for ~2–3 weeks rather than reverting toward the recent average.",
    "Post-spike behavior: the model often predicts pullbacks after rallies that do not materialize. Reduce/disable mean-reversion terms after a breakout + strong momentum signal; keep prices elevated instead of fading.",
    "Volatility compression: the model underestimates amplitude during rallies. Inflate deviations from the starting level (e.g., multiply projected move from t0 by >1) when recent realized volatility and momentum are both high."
  ]
}
